Hi Everyone,

Kernel version 2.6.28.10 has an issue.
I used 2.6.28.8, 2.6.28.9 and had no issues, this one appeared in 2.6.28.10
The kernel config I used had selinux enabled.
Recompiling 2.6.28.10 without selinux doesn't have a problem.
The kernel panics when rsyslogd gets started, I am using rsyslogd version 3.20.4
Actually, security/selinux/avc.c hasn't changed between version 2.6.28.9 and 2.6.28.10
Btw, it's a x86_64 kernel.
I'll include the kernel config I used.

